    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TDvuJ2KygqHcBPtkDgePBK)_\n\n## What\n- Commit 87a4fbb7 (`Add \" (ed.)\" suffix by hand`) edited `sp-litnotes-titles.el` only, so the `tangle` check is red on `main` and in every PR based on it.\n- That edit also changed the `else` branch of the suffix `if` to `\" (ed.)\"`, which adds the marker to **every** title, authors included (several `sp-litnotes-titles` tests fail with it).\n- Fix, done in the doc `docs/tangles/funct/sp-org-lint.org` and tangled: the `else` branch is `\"\"` again, and `sp-litnotes-titles-editor-suffix` now defaults to `\" (ed.)\"`. Editors (notes with `pub-editor` and no `pub-author`) get `Lee and Roe (ed.) (2014) Essays`; authors never get it; setting the option to `nil` removes the marker.\n- The doc bullets and the editor-fallback test are updated to the new default (the test also checks `nil`).\n- Behaviour change to confirm: the default marker was `nil` in `main` before your hand edit; I read your commit as wanting `(ed.)` shown for editors.\n\n## Not tested\n- Run on your vault. The tangle check passes; of the 20 `sp-litnotes-titles` tests, 15 pass here and 5 fail only because `sp-author-notes` is not on my load path (they fail the same way without my change).\n\n## Manual testing\n- [x] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 423-litnote-title-editor-suffix; git checkout 423-litnote-title-editor-suffix`, restart Emacs.\n- [ ] `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; bash tools/check-tangle.sh` → \"All tangled modules match their docs.\"\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun` (dry run, writes nothing): a note with only `pub-editor` is planned as `Names (ed.) (year) Title`; a note with `pub-author` has no `(ed.)`.\n- [ ] `(setq sp-litnotes-titles-editor-suffix nil)` and rerun the dry run: editor notes lose the marker.\n- [ ] Only then, if the plan looks right, apply the conversion to one note first.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDWYwkgX4eqm2SVoTC)_",
